WEBVTT

00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:04.230
How are you doing, Koto?

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:07.400
Cried any condiments lately?

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.540
Nope, I'm fine.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:10.220
Good.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.610
There don't seem to be any problems.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.170
I'll schedule your next checkup 
for three months from now.

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:16.620
What? No way.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.330
I wanna see you more often.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.870
You're welcome to come hang out anytime.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.470
Maintain an appropriate 
distance from your patients.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:31.500
Stop indiscriminately 
empathizing with everybody.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:35.720
If you can't do that, then you should close 
your mysterious disease clinic this instant.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:40.040
Otherwise, you'll make the people 
around you unhappy, too.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:41.610
Doctor?

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.640
Those three months will fly by.

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:48.670
Thank you.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.230
Thanks.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:56.330
Once I stop having regular checkups, 
I won't get to see the doctor anymore...

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:02.680
Take care.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.500
<b>Mysterious Disease Specialist</b>

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:09.790
Koto... making good progress.

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:14.780
All right. Let's get <i>your</i> 
checkup started next.

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:43.350
<b>Dr. Ramune
Mysterious Disease Specialist</b>

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:48.770
<b>Medical History Form</b>

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:48.770
<b>Name: Kuromori Toru</b>

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:48.780
Felt any nausea lately?

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:53.110
<b>Episode 12 - "Dr. Ramune -Mysterious Disease Specialist-"</b>

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:49.910
No.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:52.260
Have you been sleeping well?

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:53.100
Yes.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:03.410
I'm so glad you've filled out.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.500
You were so scrawny a year ago.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.550
Mommy's glad you've grown so quickly.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:09.090
Ow!

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:10.860
I'm not your son.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.950
There don't seem to be any problems.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.970
Recently you've even been eating out,

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:18.810
and you can eat without mixing 
medication into your food.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:19.500
Yes.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:23.630
Which means you've make a complete recovery.

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:27.060
You've done well this past year, Toru.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:30.050
Thank you.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:32.900
Sure thing.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.350
All right, let's celebrate.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.730
I'll make you whatever you want.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:42.370
What do you want to eat?

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:43.730
In that case...

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.540
Kuro, cook five cups of rice.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:47.230
Okay.

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:52.570
Anyway, why do you want katsudon again?

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:55.040
Remember what you said back then?

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:59.040
Since I'm perfectly healthy, 
I'll be eating this katsudon!

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:04.710
Once your stomach is better, 
you'll be able to eat this, too.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:07.500
I'm surprised you remember that.

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:11.070
Couldn't you eat this whenever
 you want, though?

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:12.150
It's fine.

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:16.900
I prayed I'd be able to eat 
this once I got better.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:20.680
I see. Well, it's certainly important.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.930
Thanks for the food.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.370
How's the katsudon of your prayers?

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:42.380
It's really good.

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:44.310
Glad to hear it.

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:51.470
<i>How unusual. He's smiling.</i>

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:52.540
More, please.

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:55.180
That was quick!

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.850
Well, I should get going.

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:01.840
Okay.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:07.450
Doctor.

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:09.920
What's up?

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:14.830
Since I've fully recovered, would you prefer 
if I stopped coming starting tomorrow?

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:20.420
I figured treating me must have been 
a burden on you this whole time.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.930
Huh?! What are you talking about?

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:26.810
Obviously not! Don't worry about it.

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:31.760
In that case, is it all right 
if I keep coming by?

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:33.430
Of course it is!

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:36.240
You're my assistant.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:39.370
Maintain an appropriate 
distance from your patients.

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:42.440
Stop indiscriminately 
empathizing with everybody.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:49.000
But, uh, you don't have to 
force yourself to come, okay?

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:53.600
You know, since you've 
made a complete recovery.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:57.700
And I can't guarantee working for 
me won't expose you to danger.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.130
I see.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:06.820
Wait, uh...

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:08.230
Excuse me.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:17.180
Akatsuki

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:17.170
Kuro!

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:19.620
Why won't you come back?

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:23.690
Now that you're better, 
are you done with me?

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:27.570
Without you, I'm going to die from 
loneliness and overworking myself!

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:30.170
You ungrateful monster!

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.450
What are you talking about?

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:33.950
You're the one who said he didn't
 have to keep showing up.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:35.610
You're an idiot.

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:38.700
You'll never find anyone as good as him.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:42.540
I know that better than anyone!

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:46.660
Come on, Ramu-chan.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:49.560
Have some cinnamon royal milk tea.

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:50.580
It'll calm you down.

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:53.590
Thank you, Nico-nii!

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:02.620
That certainly doesn't 
sound like you, though.

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:04.850
Why did you tell him that?

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:07.740
Well, actually...

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:15.980
You don't have to force yourself to come.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:30.020
Momiji-san!

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:32.830
Hey, kid.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:35.600
What are you doing here?

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:38.460
I have some business here.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:42.850
Uh, I think it's in that direction.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:49.330
Shall I show you the way?

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.620
No, thank you.

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:52.610
But...

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:58.460
I doubt someone who's lost can 
show another person the way.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:04.590
Tell me what's on your mind.

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:09.500
My idiotic apprentice is acting strange?

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:13.390
Yes. Something seems to be troubling him.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:18.560
I see.

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:26.390
The doctor's been acting absent-minded ever 
since we went to the mysterious labyrinth.

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:30.400
Momiji-san, do you know anything?

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:35.220
I knew you were a smart kid.

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:38.080
You're too smart to be his apprentice.

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:43.250
I simply told him...

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:46.320
...to quit being a mysterious 
disease specialist.

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:50.580
Why would you tell him that?

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:52.200
Why?

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:55.340
You're smart enough to know why.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:09:00.170
While protecting a patient, he badly 
injured himself and nearly died.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:05.090
The inability to maintain an appropriate 
distance from patients is fatal for a doctor.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:07.420
That's true...

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:11.870
I think you're absolutely correct, but...

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:14.630
Open your eyes already!

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:15.440
Do you want to die?!

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:19.290
What you choose to believe is up to you,

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:22.070
but none of that crap 
matters if you're <i>dead!</i>

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:26.410
If not for him, I would be...

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:31.910
Besides, despite what you told him,

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:35.990
I doubt he'd stop empathizing 
with his patients

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:39.800
to the point of sacrificing 
himself that easily.

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:43.460
He's an incorrigible idiot.

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:47.910
What?

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:53.590
But that's precisely why it's another matter 
if someone gets hurt because of him.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.660
Maintain an appropriate 
distance from your patients.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:59.580
Stop indiscriminately 
empathizing with everybody.

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:03.780
Otherwise, you'll make the people 
around you unhappy, too.

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:05.790
I will?

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:09.920
Especially now that you have an apprentice.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:14.150
I heard he injured himself imitating you.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:20.550
He put himself in danger in order to cure 
his friend's mysterious disease.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:25.180
If I hadn't been injured,
 I would've handled it.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:31.320
You're not understanding what 
I'm trying to tell you.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:37.330
What you're achieving through your 
own self-sacrifice isn't treatment.

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:41.620
Your patients won't pay anything 
other than your doctor's fee.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:45.100
What's unbalanced will tear at the seams.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:51.100
If you keep doing what you're doing, 
eventually you'll break.

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:54.530
And you'll bring your patients, your 
apprentice... everything down with you.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:00.370
Momiji is right.

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:06.350
It's not even self-sacrifice. 
It's self-satisfaction.

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:13.180
What if you die doing something reckless 
in an attempt to cure someone?

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:16.500
How would the person you cured feel?

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:18.720
I wouldn't want that.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:22.210
If something happened to you because of me,

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:26.320
I'd feel pain and regret 
for the rest of my life.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:30.400
So, what are you going to do?

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:32.580
Will you shut down your clinic?

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:35.890
I can't do that!

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:37.830
I have patients who'd be screwed without me!

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:40.110
Will you change your methods, then?

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:44.720
Can you avoid empathizing with your patients 
and maintain an appropriate distance?

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:48.980
Can you be like Momiji?

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:55.520
Aw, man! What am I supposed to do?!

00:11:57.030 --> 00:12:01.440
<i>I finally figured out why the 
doctor's been acting strange.</i>

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:04.780
<i>Anyone would be after what he was told.</i>

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:07.980
<i>But I think Momiji-san is right, too.</i>

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:10.930
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:15.060
Kuropi, I forgot my textbook.

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:16.930
I'm in quite the pickle.

00:12:16.930 --> 00:12:18.140
Yeah, yeah.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:32.560
Aona, have you forgotten 
whose textbook this is?

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.140
You two, we're in class!

00:12:37.350 --> 00:12:41.400
Aona's always getting in trouble,
but it's rare for him to get yelled at.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:44.020
They've been getting along well recently.

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:52.290
<b>Winner</b>

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:54.500
Look, Kuropi.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:56.250
<b>Winner</b>

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:56.250
<b>Winner</b>

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:09.020
Aona, what was that for?!

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:12.510
You seem troubled, so I'm 
charging your courage.

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:22.030
Aona, I enjoy seeing the things you make.

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:25.450
So, why don't you make something?

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:33.240
You helped me realize something important 
that I never would've figured out on my own.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:38.430
So I want to help you, too.

00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:39.670
Aona...

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:45.490
Kuropi?

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:47.050
Thanks, Aona!

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:58.860
<i>When we met, my first impression 
of him was terrible.</i>

00:13:58.990 --> 00:14:02.930
There you are! Boy, am I glad I found you.

00:14:02.930 --> 00:14:05.820
What do you want? Who are you? 
I'm calling the cops.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:08.690
I've caught a suspicious person! 
Please call the police!

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:10.950
Please help me!

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:16.480
I was born with the ability 
to see strange things.

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:19.950
I'm so scared.

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:21.950
Please help me.

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:25.200
Sir, this man is a suspicious person!

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:26.310
<i>But...</i>

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:29.130
Kid, let's get outta here!

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:31.930
I know exactly how you feel.

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:34.820
Believe in me.

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:37.610
What happened to your face?

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:40.900
Huh? Oh, this?

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:43.780
Just a scratch. Don't worry about it.

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:48.070
<i>He taught me something important 
that I hadn't noticed myself.</i>

00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:51.140
It's up to you to protect him.

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:53.670
Hello, it's Mr. Belly Button!

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:58.030
Ow, ow, ow! Stop bullying Mr. Belly Button!

00:14:58.030 --> 00:14:59.150
Hey, Kuro.

00:15:00.510 --> 00:15:02.820
Pull yourself together. This isn't like you.

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:04.730
Aren't you coming to help look?

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:07.590
<i>This time, I want to be the one to help him!</i>

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:24.110
Akatsuki

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:24.110
<b>One Week Later</b>

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:27.110
How's this?

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:33.620
Thank you for all the valuable 
and difficult-to-acquire items.

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:37.350
Oh, it's fine. That's our business. Right?

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:37.870
Yeah.

00:15:39.110 --> 00:15:42.350
Let me know if you acquire 
any other valuable items.

00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:44.690
Like the Cattail Flower I used the other day,

00:15:44.690 --> 00:15:48.140
everything this shop has to 
offer is the genuine article.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.850
Well, I should get going.

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:56.310
Oh, right. Do you have some time?

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:58.950
There's something I'd like to show you.

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:00.580
Could you come with me?

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:08.190
What did you want to show me?

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:10.890
Hey, what did you want to show me?

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:15.800
I thought it'd be nice to eat 
outside once in a while.

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:20.570
Wow, you made rice balls!

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:24.670
Yes. They contain pickled plum, 
salmon, bonito flakes, and seaweed.

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:26.570
I included some novelty rice balls, too.

00:16:26.570 --> 00:16:29.280
Seriously? Thanks, Kuro!

00:16:30.560 --> 00:16:35.700
But if you'd told me we were doing this, 
I would've cooked something, too.

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:38.650
Like side dishes, snacks, or dessert.

00:16:38.650 --> 00:16:40.240
We need drinks, too.

00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:41.630
Don't worry about it.

00:16:41.630 --> 00:16:45.080
But why? We came all the 
way out here for a picnic...

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:48.050
Look.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:54.900
Is that...

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:57.330
They're the people you've cured.

00:16:57.630 --> 00:17:00.070
When I told them I wanted to surprise you

00:17:00.070 --> 00:17:04.120
since you seemed to be 
feeling down, they all showed up.

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:09.990
Those who couldn't come asked 
me to give you their regards.

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:23.920
I see. So they're doing well, too.

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:29.670
It's true that your drastic treatments 
always put me on edge,

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:33.520
but you never reflect on your own behavior.

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:35.920
Frankly, I'm often angry with you.

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:38.570
<b>Stab</b>

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:38.570
<b>Stab</b>

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:38.570
<b>Stab</b>

00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:38.570
Hey.

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:46.570
But I've seen that there are some 
patients that only you can cure.

00:17:48.230 --> 00:17:51.980
It wasn't just our mysterious 
diseases that you cured.

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:05.590
If you try to sacrifice yourself 
to save someone again,

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:08.470
I'll do everything I can to stop you.

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:12.020
You don't have to do everything alone.

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:15.630
You're the one who taught me that.

00:18:15.630 --> 00:18:16.640
Kuro...

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:20.990
Besides, telling you to 
change will never work,

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:24.590
so it's far more realistic 
for me to help you.

00:18:24.590 --> 00:18:26.990
Hang on, what's that mean?

00:18:26.990 --> 00:18:28.400
Exactly what it sounds like.

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:30.280
And what does it sound like?!

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:33.130
Ramune really is such a softie.

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:40.180
Maybe that's the answer Ramune and 
his assistant have come up with, though.

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:43.770
Doctor!

00:18:43.770 --> 00:18:44.770
Kuropi!

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:47.670
Hurry up! We've been waiting for you!

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:49.970
Let's go.

00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:50.700
Yeah.

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:55.110
Doctor.

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:01.330
Over here. Come on, hurry up.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:02.270
You're late. We've been waiting for you.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:07.690
Momiji?

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:11.150
Give that idiot a message.

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:15.180
I'll give him a little more 
time to think things over.

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:18.740
But let me know if he ever 
feels like quitting.

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:21.460
I'd be happy to say a 
requiem for his practice.

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:25.800
Would you like to join us?

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:27.990
I have a message for <i>him</i>, too.

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:30.500
Tell him to look after 
my idiotic apprentice.

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:35.820
Goodness, he's not very honest
 about his feelings, is he?

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:40.060
Momiji-san is probably 
worried about Ramu-chan.

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:42.740
If he weren't,

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:45.690
he wouldn't play the bad guy by telling 
him to stop sacrificing himself.

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:53.930
Shall we go as well?

00:19:53.930 --> 00:19:55.490
Yes, Grandma.

00:19:57.890 --> 00:19:59.850
Whoa!

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:02.520
What a feast!

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:07.640
Thanks for the food!

00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:11.280
So good!

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:18.740
This is cute.

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:21.780
Food tastes better when 
you're eating with friends.

00:20:22.410 --> 00:20:25.170
You've improved again, Nico.

00:20:27.300 --> 00:20:29.150
What are you doing? You're creeping me out.

00:20:29.630 --> 00:20:34.920
I was just thinking I've been paid 
way more than my doctor's fee.

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:37.130
Oh, right. Kuro.

00:20:37.850 --> 00:20:41.910
Now that you've made a complete recovery, 
I'm going to train you even harder.

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:46.080
As your master, the exceedingly 
handsome and fashionable Dr. Ramune,

00:20:46.080 --> 00:20:49.440
popular with men and women of all ages.

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:54.660
Maybe you should close down your practice 
and start over from square one.

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:09.540
<i>Minds afflicted by stress 
or obsession are sometimes</i>

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:15.050
<i>afflicted by something "mysterious" 
and develop a "mysterious disease."</i>

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:18.380
<i>The "mysterious" cannot be 
seen by ordinary people.</i>

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:23.460
<i>However, as long as there are people in 
this world and those people have hearts,</i>

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:26.970
<b>Mysterious Disease Specialist</b>

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:26.590
<i>there will be those who suffer 
from bizarre diseases.</i>

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:33.570
<i>And where there are mysterious diseases, 
there are also those who cure them.</i>

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:38.260
<i>Doctors who expose the secret causes 
hidden in people's sick hearts</i>

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:42.980
<i>and save them.</i>

00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:50.140
Don't worry. I'll cure you.

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:55.000
<b>Dr. Ramune
Mysterious Disease Specialist</b>
